// A packed fleet's headings on the way (the player, 2026-11-11: battleships sailing one way, some of them turned
// sideways - "they all travel in the same direction but some get shoved sideways"): Small Islands (map seed 1,
// start_epoch 9), 24 dreadnoughts packed at 56,16 in the open north sea, sent east to 74,14, turned back west to
// 50,20 while under way, then on to 72,22 while under way again; every ship logged every step (`fmove watch`,
// # fmwatch: position, heading, speed, push). How far a ship's heading is off the way it actually moves:
// scripts/results/fleet_heading.py.
wait_until(0.1min)
spawn(1, unit.s10_dreadnought_battleship, 56, 16, 24)
wait_until(0.3min)
cmd("fmove go 1 56 16 9 74 14")
cmd("fmove watch 1")
wait_until(0.8min)
cmd("fmove go 1 64 15 12 50 20")
wait_until(1.6min)
cmd("fmove go 1 56 18 12 72 22")
wait_until(3.0min)
cmd("fmove sum")
cmd("fmove watch 0")
